  <section class="wrap fiche-body">
    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>Clinique Vétérinaire Saint-Antoine, set up at Espace Perdrigons on route de Pégomas in Grasse, has a full technical platform: consultations, surgery, analysis lab, radiology and ultrasound. It's one of the town's leading vet practices, well rated (around 4.7/5 across ~376 reviews according to one aggregator).</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>The clinic is open Monday to Friday from 8am to 7:30pm and Saturday from 8am to 6pm; it is closed on Sunday. On emergency status, our research clearly conflicts: one directory lists "24/7 emergencies" among the services offered, but another independent source explicitly states that emergencies are transferred to another facility (not identified in our sources, likely a dedicated local structure), mentioning 3115 (the national number connecting to an on-call vet) for Sundays and public holidays. This signal points towards care not being handled directly by the clinic itself outside hours — we therefore do not give it a "24/7 Emergencies" badge. A call before heading over outside opening hours remains essential.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: keep the clinic's number handy during your stay in Grasse, and always call before heading over outside the listed opening hours.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Grasse, the perfume capital of the world, and its historic centre are just a few minutes' drive from the clinic.</p>
